Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:39:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(kanban):=20central=20sync=20client=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20shadow=20mode,=20import,=20diff=20(phase=202)=20[da?=
 =?UTF-8?q?veey]?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 2 of the central Kanban plan (hermes-mods core/kanban-central-service.md):
connects the phase 1 seams to the hermes-hub Board service.

- hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py: pull first (GET /v2/boards/<id>/changes,
  applied with the cursor in the same transaction; 410 rebuilds from paged
  /snapshot), then push the capture-trigger outbox as row ops (POST /ops,
  HLC-stamped here, FIFO batches of 200). applied/merged clear the row;
  rejected marks it and, on a primary board, restores the service's row.
  Fields with an unanswered local edit are not overwritten by a pull.
  Identity is the gateway's hub enrollment (~/.config/hermes-mail), or
  kanban.sync.{url,key_file,gateway}. HubLeaseClient implements the phase 1
  LeaseClient over POST /leases (claim_gate now passes the review lane).
- shadow mode: the live board's outbox is pushed, but the feed is applied
  only into <root>/kanban/sync-shadow/<board>.db with observers off (no hooks,
  no notifications), so the live board stays local while `sync diff` compares.
- every synced board keeps a replica of the whole board in that file; primary
  mode also applies this gateway's OWN cards from the feed into the live board
  (created_on = it, plus their child rows) and never another gateway's, so the
  dispatcher's sweeps (stale claims, orphans, concurrency) never see foreign
  work; cross-gateway reads come from the replica.
- hermes kanban sync {status,attach,import,diff,run}. import queues every
  existing row once (tasks as import: an id another gateway created is
  refused id_taken; events older than the service's 30-day retention are
  skipped). diff reports missing/extra/field/child mismatches and rejected
  ops; unpushed rows count as pending, not as differences.
- gateway: _kanban_sync_watcher runs the loop in a thread, one gateway per
  host (advisory lock), while kanban.sync.enabled is on.
- kanban_db_sync: kanban.sync is read from the kanban root's config.yaml (the
  storage is host-wide: a worker under another profile must not see sync off
  and drop the board's triggers); kanban.sync.boards selects boards (absent =
  all); server-set created_on is applied from the feed, never captured; the
  service's lease mirror is taken from the task row; set_identity binds a
  board to its service board and this gateway's hub name; an equal-version
  row is re-applied (a re-send or a revert), only older ones are skipped.
- kanban_provider_walls: read/write with an explicit encoding (scripts/check
  footguns; the file came in with 8ae2a62).

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_client.py (25) against an in-memory
fake of the Board contract (kanban_sync_fake_board.py); the phase 1 sync
suites pass except three lease tests that fail identically on the base
(live-system guard blocks a real os.kill on this host).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
